<title>RUSSIA: Russian GDP rises 0.9 pct yr/yr in February.</title>
<headline>Russian GDP rises 0.9 pct yr/yr in February.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian gross domestic product over the first two months of this year totalled 401 trillion roubles, which was 0.5 percent more than a year earlier in inflation-adjusted terms, the State Statistics Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>    RUSSIAN GDP			  Feb 97    Jan 97    Feb 96</p>
<p>    month-on-month pct change	 -2.0     -12.0	-3.0</p>
<p>    year-on-year pct change	   +0.9	+0.1	-3.0</p>
<p>February was the second successive month in which GDP rose year-on-year.</p>
<p>Note - Official Russian data tend to underreport a growing private sector in the economy.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
